# Pairs with DecisionDurability. A recorded terminal decision that can be
# rewritten is the "registry decision is not durable" defect: readers that
# already resolved against the commit see it withdrawn.
MODULE: DecisionDurabilityDecisionFlip
TARGET: DecisionDurability
CLASS: Action
SUMMARY: rewrites a recorded committed decision to aborted, so a terminal decision is not durable

--- FIND
Next ==
    \/ \E t \in Txns : PrepareTx(t)
--- REPLACE
\* MUTATION: a recorded decision can be overwritten after the fact. Left
\* deliberately unfair (it is not added to TxProgress), so it perturbs only the
\* safety property under test and cannot affect the liveness properties.
DecisionFlip(t) ==
    /\ decision[t] = "committed"
    /\ decision' = [decision EXCEPT ![t] = "aborted"]
    /\ UNCHANGED <<phase, vote, terminal, pend, orphanDone, revision>>

Next ==
    \/ \E t \in Txns : DecisionFlip(t)
    \/ \E t \in Txns : PrepareTx(t)
--- END
